   "text": {
    "L1": "When denominators match, the parts are the same size. Add or subtract the numerators and keep the denominator.",
    "L2": "When denominators differ, do not add them. First rewrite both fractions with a common denominator.",
    "L3": "For three fourths plus one sixth, twelve is a common denominator.",
    "L4": "Multiply the top and bottom of three fourths by three. It becomes nine twelfths.",
    "L5": "Multiply the top and bottom of one sixth by two. It becomes two twelfths.",
    "L6": "Now the parts match, so nine twelfths plus two twelfths is eleven twelfths. Check that it is more than three fourths and less than one.",
    "L7": "Which answer is correct for one half plus one third? Tap it."
   },
